  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe TrustBonding contract uses a utilization ratio to scale user rewards. If a user's utilization delta is less than or equal to zero (meaning they did not actively increase their participation in the MultiVault), their yield is slashed to the personalUtilizationLowerBound (default 2500, or 25%).\n\nHowever, the developers explicitly intended to exempt new users from this penalty on their first claim. As noted in the comments at line 527: \"If the user had nothing claimable last epoch, don't penalize them as it's their first ever claim.\" Due to an execution ordering error in _getPersonalUtilizationRatio, this exemption is unreachable for passive stakers. The strict penalty check (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0) is evaluated before the first-claim exemption check (userUtilizationTarget == 0).\n\n## Root Cause\nWhen a new user stakes TRUST purely for yield and does not interact with the MultiVault, their rawUtilizationDelta for their first epoch mathematically evaluates to 0.\n\nWhen they attempt to make their first claim, the function evaluates rawUtilizationDelta <= 0. Because 0 <= 0 is true, the function returns early and applies the personalUtilizationLowerBound. The execution never reaches the intended exemption block.\n\nSolidity\n    // src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol\n\n    int256 rawUtilizationDelta = userUtilizationAfter - userUtilizationBefore;\n\n    // 1. Evaluated first. Slashes new passive users (whose delta is 0) instantly.\n    if (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0) {\n        return personalUtilizationLowerBound; \n    }\n\n    uint256 userUtilizationDelta = uint256(rawUtilizationDelta);\n    uint256 userUtilizationTarget = userClaimedRewardsForEpoch[_account][_epoch - 1];\n\n    // 2. Unreachable for new users whose delta was 0.\n    if (userUtilizationTarget == 0) {\n        // If the user had nothing claimable last epoch, don't penalize them as it's their first ever claim\n        if (_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(_account, _epoch - 1) == 0) {\n            return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR; \n        }\n        return personalUtilizationLowerBound;\n    }\n\n## Impact\nAny new user who locks TRUST to passively stake without interacting with the MultiVault will have up to 75% of their first epoch's matured yield permanently destroyed. This directly contradicts the protocol's explicitly documented economic design. As per Code4rena severity criteria, deterministic loss of matured yield due to incorrect logic implementation is classified as High severity.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nThe target and eligibility exemptions must be evaluated before applying the strict delta penalty. Reorder the logic blocks:\n\nSolidity\n    int256 rawUtilizationDelta = userUtilizationAfter - userUtilizationBefore;\n    uint256 userUtilizationTarget = userClaimedRewardsForEpoch[_account][_epoch - 1];\n\n    // 1. Evaluate exemptions first\n    if (userUtilizationTarget == 0) {\n        if (_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(_account, _epoch - 1) == 0) {\n            return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR; \n        }\n        return personalUtilizationLowerBound;\n    }\n\n    // 2. Apply the strict delta penalty\n    if (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0) {\n        return personalUtilizationLowerBound;\n    }\n\n    uint256 userUtilizationDelta = uint256(rawUtilizationDelta);",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept (PoC) \nThe following demonstrates that a new user who joins after the protocol's bootstrap phase (Epoch 2 or later) and passively stakes will predictably fail the rawUtilizationDelta <= 0 check and have their ratio slashed, bypassing the explicit isFirstEverClaim exemption entirely.\n\nInstructions:\nPlace this test directly inside tests/unit/TrustBonding/TrustBondingTest.t.sol (which inherits the protocol's integration setup) and run:\nforge test --match-test test_FirstClaim_ExemptionBypass_Integration -vvv\n\nSolidity\n    function test_FirstClaim_ExemptionBypass_Integration() external {\n        // 1. Advance time past the bootstrap phase. \n        // TrustBonding explicitly hardcodes a 100% ratio for Epochs 0 and 1.\n        // We advance to Epoch 2 to test the actual mathematical engine.\n        _advanceEpochs(2);\n\n        // 2. A new passive user (Bob) locks TRUST to earn yield during Epoch 2.\n        // He DOES NOT interact with the MultiVault, so his MultiVault utilization delta remains 0.\n        _createLock(users.bob);\n\n        // 3. Advance time to Epoch 3 so Bob's rewards from Epoch 2 mature.\n        _advanceEpochs(1);\n        \n        uint256 currentEpoch = protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(); // Should be 3\n        uint256 claimableEpoch = currentEpoch - 1; // Should be 2\n\n        // 4. Verify Bob is actually eligible for rewards\n        uint256 eligibleRewards = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.bob, claimableEpoch);\n        assertTrue(eligibleRewards > 0, \"Bob should be eligible for rewards\");\n\n        // 5. Fetch the actual ratio applied by the live, integrated TrustBonding contract\n        uint256 appliedRatio = protocol.trustBonding.getPersonalUtilizationRatio(users.bob, claimableEpoch);\n\n        // 6. The intended ratio for a first-time claimer is 10000 (100%).\n        // Because of the early return bug, the live contract evaluates (delta <= 0) first and applies the lower bound.\n        // Note: BaseTest configures the lower bound to 3000 (30%).\n        assertEq(appliedRatio, 3000, \"Bug: User was slashed to lower bound!\");\n        assertTrue(appliedRatio != 10000, \"Bug: First-claim exemption was bypassed!\");\n    }",
